All right, here's possibly my best idea yet (well, besides having an
awesome pet).  I have a coaligned altar at around dlvl12.  If I put my
luckstone in my bag of holding to bring my luck back down to 10, and
then bring my luck down to 6 by breaking two mirrors (or cheating 4
times in Sokoban by using wands of striking on the remaining
boulders), I will have a 1-in-6 chance of gaining an additional point
of protection each time I pray on an altar.  The reasoning behind
bringing luck down to 6 is to remove two possible outcomes from
prayer, getting a spellbook (worthless to an illiterate) and getting
crowned (bad!).

So yes, I guess I would end up doing some pudding farming, but I'd
rather farm puddings for divine protection than dying somewhere to a
large gang of nasties in Gehennom.

After I farm some more divine protection off black puddings, then I'll
go find a polymorph/magic trap somewhere and make some awesome pets.
And, assuming I've found a magic whistle by that point too, I should
be ready for the end game.

Sounds like a plan!


